---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';

// Equal-density contours of N(0, I) and a diagonal Gaussian with
// μ = (0.75, 0.5), σ = (0.55, 0.35), in the same two-dimensional coordinates.
const scale = 41;
const origin = { x: 170, y: 171 };
const mu = { x: origin.x + 0.75 * scale, y: origin.y - 0.5 * scale };
const sigma = { x: 0.55 * scale, y: 0.35 * scale };
const illustrativeOffsets = [[-0.8, 0.4], [0.5, -0.5], [1.2, 0.3], [-0.3, -1], [0.7, 0.8], [-0.5, 0.9]];
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Latent-space sketch"
  title="From an encoded point to a distribution over latent codes"
  caption="Reconstructed from the nearby-code sketch on page 26 and the Gaussian prior and per-input posterior sketches on pages 27–28. The axes, Gaussian contours, and KL annotation are editorial clarifications. The dots are illustrative, not measured embeddings. Reconstruction alone does not specify a sampling prior; the VAE regularizes each qφ(z|x) toward its chosen prior, without guaranteeing that the aggregate encoded distribution equals that prior."
>
  <div class="latent-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 350" role="img" aria-labelledby="vae-latent-ae-title vae-latent-ae-desc">
      <title id="vae-latent-ae-title">A deterministic autoencoder has reference codes but no prescribed sampling prior</title>
      <desc id="vae-latent-ae-desc">One encoded reference point has several nearby latent points. A separate arbitrary point lies in a region between the depicted codes. The drawing illustrates that reconstruction training alone does not specify where to sample latent vectors, rather than claiming that every arbitrary sample must fail.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="vae-latent-ae-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrow-head" /></marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="170" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Deterministic autoencoder</text>
      <text x="170" y="45" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">A reference code and its neighborhood</text>
      <path d="M 44 65 V 275 H 302" class="axis" marker-end="url(#vae-latent-ae-arrow)" />
      <path d="M 44 86 V 63" class="axis" marker-end="url(#vae-latent-ae-arrow)" />
      <text x="31" y="76" text-anchor="end" class="axis-label">z₂</text><text x="306" y="270" class="axis-label">z₁</text>
      <ellipse cx="144" cy="175" rx="39" ry="34" class="neighborhood" />
      <g class="nearby-point"><circle cx="128" cy="161" r="4" /><circle cx="158" cy="164" r="4" /><circle cx="157" cy="191" r="4" /><circle cx="129" cy="188" r="4" /></g>
      <circle cx="141" cy="176" r="5" class="reference-point" />
      <text x="82" y="107" class="annotation">Encoded z<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">ref</tspan></text>
      <path d="M 118 116 L 138 167" class="callout" />
      <text x="106" y="239" class="muted">Nearby codes</text><path d="M 143 222 V 212" class="callout" />
      <circle cx="250" cy="105" r="26" class="gap" />
      <path d="M 245 100 L 255 110 M 255 100 L 245 110" class="arbitrary-point" />
      <path d="M 250 136 V 143" class="callout" />
      <text x="250" y="164" text-anchor="middle">Arbitrary z</text>
      <text x="250" y="186" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Untrained gap</text>
      <text x="170" y="311" text-anchor="middle" class="summary">Reconstruction alone does not choose p(z).</text>
      <text x="170" y="333" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Coverage depends on the learned codes.</text>
    </svg>

    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 350" role="img" aria-labelledby="vae-latent-vae-title vae-latent-vae-desc">
      <title id="vae-latent-vae-title">A VAE uses a standard normal prior and a Gaussian approximate posterior for each input</title>
      <desc id="vae-latent-vae-desc">Two circular equal-density contours depict the prior N(0,I). Two elliptical equal-density contours depict a diagonal Gaussian q phi of z given one input x, with mean (0.75,0.5) and standard deviations (0.55,0.35). The highlighted mean and example sample points belong to that input's approximate posterior. A KL regularizer compares q phi of z given x to the chosen prior.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="vae-latent-vae-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrow-head" /></marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="170" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Variational autoencoder</text>
      <text x="170" y="45" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">One distribution qφ(z|x) for this input</text>
      <path d="M 44 65 V 275 H 302" class="axis" marker-end="url(#vae-latent-vae-arrow)" />
      <path d="M 44 86 V 63" class="axis" marker-end="url(#vae-latent-vae-arrow)" />
      <text x="31" y="76" text-anchor="end" class="axis-label">z₂</text><text x="306" y="270" class="axis-label">z₁</text>
      <g class="prior-contours"><circle cx={origin.x} cy={origin.y} r={scale} /><circle cx={origin.x} cy={origin.y} r={2 * scale} /></g>
      <g class="posterior-contours"><ellipse cx={mu.x} cy={mu.y} rx={sigma.x} ry={sigma.y} /><ellipse cx={mu.x} cy={mu.y} rx={2 * sigma.x} ry={2 * sigma.y} /></g>
      <g class="posterior-point">{illustrativeOffsets.map(([a, b]) => <circle cx={mu.x + a * sigma.x} cy={mu.y - b * sigma.y} r="3" />)}</g>
      <circle cx={mu.x} cy={mu.y} r="4.5" class="reference-point" />
      <text x="62" y="77">p(z) = N(0, I)</text><path d="M 113 83 L 118 108" class="callout" />
      <text x="285" y="92" text-anchor="end" class="annotation">qφ(z|x)</text><path d="M 265 100 L 231 126" class="posterior-callout" />
      <text x="258" y="212" text-anchor="middle" class="annotation">μ(x)</text><path d="M 249 199 L 206 157" class="posterior-callout" />
      <text x="170" y="306" text-anchor="middle" class="summary">KL(qφ(z|x) || p(z))</text>
      <text x="170" y="329" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Regularize each input's distribution toward the prior.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .latent-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-size: 15px; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 17px; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .axis-label { font-size: 16px; font-style: italic; }
  .subscript { font-size: 10px; }
  .summary { font-size: 14px; }
  .annotation { fill: var(--accent); }
  .axis, .arrow-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.3; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .callout { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; }
  .posterior-callout { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1; }
  .neighborhood, .gap { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-dasharray: 4 4; }
  .nearby-point { fill: var(--ink); }
  .reference-point, .posterior-point { fill: var(--accent); }
  .arbitrary-point { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .prior-contours { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .posterior-contours { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .latent-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; } svg { max-width: 390px; margin-inline: auto; } }
</style>
